cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: "LoFi: calibration-free KV cache compression via low-frequency RoPE channels"
abstract: >-
  LoFi separates position-invariant low-frequency RoPE channels from
  position-dependent high-frequency channels at the sqrt(base) boundary, uses
  the low-frequency channels to select token pairs for merging, and applies a
  mass-corrected content-preserving merge so that a surviving cache slot keeps
  both the content and the attention mass of the tokens folded into it. No
  calibration data is required.
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
